ageCode":"dz","languageName":{"simpleText":"دزونكا"}},{"languageCode":"qu","languageName":{"simpleText":"كيشوا"}},{"languageCode":"haw","languageName":{"simpleText":"لغة هاواي"}},{"languageCode":"kri","languageName":{"simpleText":"Kri"}}],"defaultAudioTrackIndex":0}},"videoDetails":{"videoId":"bQTc72t64z0","title":"What is WiFi 6? Fastest WiFi? Learn about New AX WiFi Routers from TP-Link!","lengthSeconds":"140","keywords":["ax wifi","802.11ax","next gen wifi","archer ax6000","archer ax11000","tplink ax wifi","tplink ax6000","tplink ax11000","wifi 6","fast wifi router","fast wifi","best wifi router","tplink wifi","fastest wifi router","fastest wifi","best wifi router 2019","Mu Mimo Routers","wifi router","best wifi router for home","wifi speed","axwifi","wifi6","what is wifi 6"],"channelId":"UCbdQjm1J3gIJ2E_2Yq6nxlQ","isOwnerViewing":false,"shortDescription":"Learn More about WiFi 6 by TP-Link: https://www.tp-link.com/us/wifi6/best-wifi6-router/\n\nWhat is WiFi 6? (also known as AX WiFi)  \n \nWiFi 6 is the next generation standard in WiFi technology. WiFi 6 also known as “AX WiFi or 802.11 ax WiFi” builds and improves on the current 802.11ac WiFi standard. \nWiFi 6 was originally built in response to the growing number of devices in the world. If you own a VR device, multiple smart home devices, or simply have a large number of devices in your household, then a WiFi 6 router might just be the best WiFi router for you. \n\nAX WiFi uses both 1024 QAM to provide a signal packed with more data (giving you more efficiency) and a 160 MHz Channel to provide a wider channel to make your WiFi faster. Experience stutter-free VR or enjoy stunningly vivid 4K and even 8K streaming. \n\nWiFi 6 uses 8x8 uplink/downlink, MU-MIMO, OFDMA, and BSS Color to provide up to 4x larger capacity and to handle more devices. \n\nLearn more about WiFi 6 here: http://bit.ly/AXWIFIYT","isCrawlable":true,"thumbnail":{"thumbnails":[{"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bQTc72t64z0/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaym