000#M$M#rs$AOn4CLBffmfw92-V5kJDLzr8LZSldC7FbA|160#90#71#5#5#2000#M$M#rs$AOn4CLDCc5A8WxEBtt4qakjpT4alz-hb9w","recommendedLevel":2,"highResolutionRecommendedLevel":2}},"microformat":{"playerMicroformatRenderer":{"thumbnail":{"thumbnails":[{"url":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bQTc72t64z0/maxresdefault.jpg","width":1280,"height":720}]},"embed":{"iframeUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/bQTc72t64z0","width":1280,"height":720},"title":{"simpleText":"What is WiFi 6? Fastest WiFi? Learn about New AX WiFi Routers from TP-Link!"},"description":{"simpleText":"Learn More about WiFi 6 by TP-Link: https://www.tp-link.com/us/wifi6/best-wifi6-router/\n\nWhat is WiFi 6? (also known as AX WiFi)  \n \nWiFi 6 is the next generation standard in WiFi technology. WiFi 6 also known as “AX WiFi or 802.11 ax WiFi” builds and improves on the current 802.11ac WiFi standard. \nWiFi 6 was originally built in response to the growing number of devices in the world. If you own a VR device, multiple smart home devices, or simply have a large number of devices in your household, then a WiFi 6 router might just be the best WiFi router for you. \n\nAX WiFi uses both 1024 QAM to provide a signal packed with more data (giving you more efficiency) and a 160 MHz Channel to provide a wider channel to make your WiFi faster. Experience stutter-free VR or enjoy stunningly vivid 4K and even 8K streaming. \n\nWiFi 6 uses 8x8 uplink/downlink, MU-MIMO, OFDMA, and BSS Color to provide up to 4x larger capacity and to handle more devices. \n\nLearn more about WiFi 6 here: http://bit.ly/AXWIFIYT"},"lengthSeconds":"140","ownerProfileUrl":"http://www.youtube.com/@TPLINKUS","externalChannelId":"UCbdQjm1J3gIJ2E_2Yq6nxlQ","isFamilySafe":true,"availableCountries":["AD","AE","AF","AG","AI","AL","AM","AO","AQ","AR","AS","AT","AU","AW","AX","AZ","BA","BB","BD","BE","BF","BG","BH","BI","BJ","BL","BM","BN","BO","BQ","BR","BS","BT","BV","BW","BY","BZ","CA","CC","CD","CF","CG","CH","CI","CK","CL","CM","CN","CO","CR","CU","CV","CW","CX"